  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 103.07 Food waste",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 103.07 “Food waste” means “food waste” as defined in RSA 149-M:4, IX-a, namely “the organic residues generated by the handling, preparation, storage, sale, and serving of foods and beverages. ‘Food waste’ includes pre-consumer and post-consumer organic residues, food scraps, and non-petroleum oil used for food preparation provided it does not contain sanitary wastewater.”\n\nSource. #14103, effective 10-23-24 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw100.html"
